A04s (Metal track M1c): keep a uniform/FAU value or a constant out of CLPER's source 0.

Bifrost's CLPER reads source 0 from a register port only (bi_pack_add_clper_i32 asserts
(1 << src0) & 0x7). nir_lower_subgroups' shuffle loop reads load_subgroup_invocation through
read_invocation; Bifrost emits the invocation as a MOV of the lane-id FAU value, copy
propagation folded it into CLPER, and a Metal simd_sum() compiled for the Mali-G52 (v7)
failed to pack. With BIFROST_MESA_DEBUG=noopt it compiled, which pointed at the optimiser.
Mesa 25.0.7. Ours, under Mesa's licence for the file it changes (MIT).

--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bi_opt_copy_prop.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bi_opt_copy_prop.c
@@ -107,6 +107,19 @@
          if (repl.type == BI_INDEX_CONSTANT && bi_reads_fau(ins))
             continue;
 
+         /* CLPER reads its source 0 from a register port only
+          * (bi_pack_add_clper_i32: (1 << src0) & 0x7), so a uniform, a
+          * special FAU value such as the lane ID, or a constant must not be
+          * propagated there: nir_lower_subgroups' shuffle loop reads
+          * load_subgroup_invocation through read_invocation, which became
+          * CLPER.i32 lane-id and failed to pack on Bifrost v7.
+          */
+         if ((ins->op == BI_OPCODE_CLPER_I32 ||
+              ins->op == BI_OPCODE_CLPER_OLD_I32) &&
+             s == 0 &&
+             (repl.type == BI_INDEX_FAU || repl.type == BI_INDEX_CONSTANT))
+            continue;
+
          if (!bi_is_null(repl))
             bi_replace_src(ins, s, repl);
       }
